      <span class="last-updated">Last updated: June 2026</span>

      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>BikeLabs ("we", "us", "our") operates the website at bikelabs.com (the "Site"). We are committed to protecting your privacy. This policy explains what data is collected when you visit BikeLabs, how it is used, and the choices you have.</p>
      <p>By using the Site you agree to the practices described in this policy. If you do not agree, please discontinue use of the Site.</p>

      <h2>What Data We Collect</h2>
      <p>BikeLabs does not require you to create an account or submit any personal information to browse the Site. The data collected falls into two categories:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Analytics data</strong> — if Google Analytics is active on the Site, it collects anonymised information such as pages visited, time on page, browser type, device type, and approximate geographic location (country/city level). Individual users are not personally identified.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising data</strong> — Google AdSense and its partners may collect data via cookies and similar technologies to serve advertisements. This may include your IP address, browser identifiers, and browsing behaviour across sites that use Google advertising services.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not collect your name, email address, payment information, or any other directly identifying personal data unless you voluntarily contact us at info@bikelabs.com, in which case we store only the information you provide in order to reply.</p>

      <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>We use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the Site so we can improve our content. Google Analytics uses cookies to track sessions and generate anonymised reports. The data is processed by Google LLC. You can opt out of Google Analytics tracking by installing the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.</p>
      <p>For more information on how Google uses data from our site, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's partner policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Google AdSense &amp; Personalised Advertising</h2>
      <p>BikeLabs uses Google AdSense to display advertisements. AdSense uses the DoubleClick cookie and other tracking technologies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests, based on your browsing activity across websites that participate in the Google Display Network.</p>
      <p>Personalised advertising means Google may use information from your browser or device to show you ads more likely to be relevant to you. This is governed by Google's own privacy policy, which you can review at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>
      <p>To opt out of personalised advertising from Google, visit <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a>. You can also opt out of interest-based advertising from participating companies through the <a href="https://www.networkadvertising.org/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Network Advertising Initiative</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Digital Advertising Alliance</a> opt-out tools.</p>

      <h2>Amazon Associates Programme</h2>
      <p>BikeLabs participates in the Amazon Associates Programme, an affiliate advertising programme designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by linking to Amazon. When you click an affiliate link on BikeLabs and make a purchase, we may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you.</p>
      <p>Clicking an Amazon affiliate link will take you to Amazon's website, which operates under its own privacy policy. Amazon may set cookies on your device to track the referral. Please review <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=468496" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Amazon's Privacy Notice</a> for details on how Amazon handles your data.</p>
      <p>We only recommend products we genuinely believe are useful to our readers. Affiliate links are disclosed where they appear and do not affect our editorial opinions.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>Cookies are small text files placed on your device by websites you visit. BikeLabs itself does not set first-party cookies beyond those required for basic site functionality. Third-party cookies may be set by Google AdSense, Google Analytics, and Amazon as described above.</p>
      <p>You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings. Disabling cookies may affect the functionality of some features on this and other websites. For guidance on managing cookies, visit <a href="https://www.allaboutcookies.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">allaboutcookies.org</a>.</p>

      <h2>No Sale of Personal Data</h2>
      <p>BikeLabs does not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to any third party. The only data shared with third parties is what is automatically collected by Google Analytics, Google AdSense, and Amazon Associates as described in this policy, each of which operates under its own data-processing terms.</p>

      <h2>Data Retention</h2>
      <p>We retain email correspondence for as long as necessary to respond to and resolve your query, typically no more than 12 months. Analytics and advertising data retained by Google is subject to Google's own retention policies.</p>

      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights regarding your personal data, including the right to access, correct, or request deletion of data we hold about you. To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at info@bikelabs.com. We will respond within a reasonable timeframe.</p>
      <p>For data processed by Google or Amazon, you should exercise your rights directly with those companies through their respective privacy portals.</p>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>BikeLabs is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information to us, please contact us at info@bikelabs.com and we will delete it promptly.</p>

      <h2>Links to Third-Party Sites</h2>
      <p>The Site may contain links to external websites including Amazon, manufacturer sites, and other publishers. BikeLabs is not responsible for the privacy practices of those sites. We encourage you to review the privacy policy of any third-party site you visit.</p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this privacy policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or applicable law. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page will reflect any revisions. Continued use of the Site after any changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

      <h2>Jurisdiction &amp; Governing Law</h2>
      <p>This privacy policy is governed by applicable law. We aim to comply with all major data protection regulations including GDPR (EU), CCPA (California), and other applicable privacy laws. If you have a concern about how your data is handled, please contact us at <a href="mailto:info@bikelabs.com">info@bikelabs.com</a> and we will work to resolve it promptly.</p>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have any questions, concerns or requests regarding this privacy policy or the way we handle your data, please reach out to us:</p>
      <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:info@bikelabs.com">info@bikelabs.com</a></p>

